<!--
  Layer-2 integration fixture (2026-07-22) for lotar_uri_resolve_check.py's _fmu_root_via_extra():
  demonstrates the corrected FMU-root resolution base for fmi-ls-ref's Related/@source. This file
  is deliberately packaged at the real "extra/org.fmi-standard.fmi-ls-ref/" location relative to
  the enclosing lotar-fmi-ls-ref-archive-test-VALID/ directory, which stands in for an unzipped
  FMU root (sibling documentation/ and results/ directories, as a real FMU's resources/,
  documentation/, sources/, modelDescription.xml would sit). Both Related/@source values below are
  relative to that FMU root, NOT to this manifest's own extra/org.fmi-standard.fmi-ls-ref/
  directory — confirming they resolve up through "extra/" correctly rather than being (wrongly)
  looked for at extra/org.fmi-standard.fmi-ls-ref/documentation/UserGuide.pdf etc. Checksums are
  real SHA3-256 digests of the actual sibling files, so this also exercises full checksum
  verification, not just path resolution.
-->
